The logic stays the same. The rewrite reads `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals once, so the compiler can keep them in registers instead of reloading the members after each check. The null check, bounds check and returned value are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* const p = profile;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if ((p != NULL) && (idx < p->numFields))
        return p->fields[idx].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```